  "boundary_rationale": {
    "3": "Combine the opening doubt with the need for action; distinguish reciprocity from the sustaining wheel; connect freedom to exemplary action before moving to agency, duty and desire.",
    "4": "Keep the birth question and reply together, then divine manifestation; follow action/inaction into the sage, sacrifices, the teacher, purifying knowledge and the final call to cut doubt.",
    "5": "Bring the two paths into one opening; group the lotus image with non-doership, purification with the nine-gated city, knowledge with equal vision, and inward joy with the path to peace.",
    "6": "Distinguish preparation from meditative experience, and peaceful practice from equal vision. Separate Arjuna’s failure question from Kṛṣṇa’s reassurance, retaining recovered insight with former practice.",
    "7": "Retain the already coherent opening turns. Split the final seven-verse passage at the real contrast: delusion in 24–27, freedom and knowledge at death in 28–30.",
    "8": "Join questions to definitions; keep ongoing remembrance with the final thought. Move verse 16 into the cosmic-return unit, rather than leaving it with the no-return practice.",
    "9": "Follow cosmic support, misunderstanding, true worship, the Lord’s universality, finite versus devoted destinations, offering, and the inclusive final promise.",
    "10": "Keep recognition separate from the request for meditation aids. Break the long catalogue at a change of subject: beings/powers, then time/language/life/death. Join the seed to the concluding summary.",
    "11": "Preserve changes of speaker and emotional turns: request, vision, awe, fear, destruction, Time’s reply, hymn, apology, request for the gentle form, restoration and devotion.",
    "12": "Bring the manifest/unmanifest comparison together; join deliverance with the instruction to focus the heart. Keep the practice ladder intact and give the devotee’s qualities two memorable turns.",
    "13": "Replace fourteen fragments with six teaching turns: field, preparation for knowledge, knowable Brahman, nature/experiencer, paths to equal vision, and the untouched Self. Keep the complete Brahman portrait together.",
    "14": "Group the binding mechanisms, prevailing signs and consequences separately, rather than giving each two-verse observation its own theme. Preserve Arjuna’s question, the witness’s marks and devotion as distinct turns.",
    "15": "Keep cutting the tree with seeking its source; group the whole soul-journey and its recognition. Join light, nourishment, digestion and knowledge as divine sustenance; gather the three-person distinction and conclusion.",
    "16": "Make the five turns explicit: contrasting natures, false worldview, craving/boast, empty worship and downfall, then the practical exit. Never split the continuous self-boast in 13–15.",
    "18": "Gather the opening definition and retained duties; complete the five-causes discussion before the knowledge classification. Pair action with doer, separate preparation for Brahman from mature devotion, and keep reflection before the final secret."
  }
